From c793f47d0d48ab9044f7d6419a6aae81fcc02c3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:00:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox, settings_ui: a jail logs in with a kyomei
 account
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next §6.65 and the first step of §6.70. Since 0141 each jailed project has its own
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, so every new project -- and every new worktree, whose canonical root is a new
state folder -- asks for a Claude login of its own. Sharing one login is not the fix: Anthropic's
refresh token is single-use, so two copies of a credential kill each other, and a shared or
bind-mounted file breaks because Claude Code saves by renaming over it.

Decided 2026-11-22 (operator): wait for kyomei, used the way Claude Swap is, delivering into a
thread's config dir only the token that logs it in. Asked again 2026-11-28 (operator): "use an
existing account inside kyomei or connect a new one", done directly.

- `agent_sandbox.account` (the default) and `agent_sandbox.projects[root].account` name a kyomei
  account -- a slot number, an alias or an e-mail. Unset leaves each project its own login, as
  before; a project's empty string is its own login under a default account.
- Before each jailed start, `jail_account::deliver` runs `kyomei deliver <account> --config-dir
  <project>/claude --json`. kyomei renews the account if it has under an hour left and writes a
  badge -- the access token with no refreshToken key -- merged key by key under Claude Code's three
  locks. Without the key Claude Code uses the token and never touches the file (kyomei briefing
  09, R9); a placeholder would make it blank the token. Zeo reads back only the account number,
  its e-mail and the expiry; kyomei's stderr is never read.
- A delivery that fails refuses the start (`LaunchCause::Account`, cause=account), naming the
  reason: kyomei missing, blocked (a lock held, or the account quarantined after invalid_grant),
  timed out, or an answer of another schema version. Starting anyway would land on Claude's login
  screen with no word of why.
- `agent_sandbox.kyomei_path` (unset: PATH). The account and the path are in the settings
  fingerprint, so a new choice shows the lock's restart (0057, §6.50).
- The Agent Sandbox page gets a Claude account block beside the secrets: one switch per kyomei
  account plus the project's own login, exactly one on; "Use the default account"; "Connect a new
  account…", which runs `kyomei add` in a terminal of the workspace -- a fresh login in a scratch
  directory, a token family of its own, which kyomei stores and deletes the scratch copy of -- and
  reads the list again when it ends; and Refresh.
- Messages in the nine languages.

Measured live on 2026-11-28 with a real login, Claude Code 2.1.332: a badge alone answers a
`claude -p` turn and the file is left untouched (R9 holds); kyomei's renewal against the real
endpoint rotates, and a second one succeeds, so the rotated token was persisted; a renewal
REVOKES the previous access token ("OAuth token revoked"), so every directory of the account is
redelivered at once; and a running session whose token was revoked and rewritten under it
answered its next turn -- Claude Code re-reads the file. A long session therefore survives a
renewal without a restart.

Tests: agent_sandbox `jail_account_tests` (default, own choice, opt-out, schema version, exit 3,
argv of a fake kyomei); settings_ui `agent_jail_account_tests` (rows, one switch on, a choice
kyomei no longer holds, quarantine note, toggling off falls back to the own login).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
